From d803e6f7c8120f4cd5ff5f497f472ca41b599ca2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 16 Aug 2026 17:59:46 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] Allow shifts to cross midnight (e.g. 20:00-01:00)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

ShiftFormModal blocked any end time not strictly after the start time,
making late-night shifts impossible. End <= start now means "ends the
next day" instead of being rejected — matches how the form's own hint
text explains it.

AdminScreen's save handler resolves the actual end date from that
rule (new addDays() helper in schedule.ts) so the stored end_time is
genuinely after start_time, satisfying the DB's shifts_time_order
check constraint instead of violating it.

Timeline's drag-to-create clamped against a hardcoded 0-1439 range and
formatted minutes without wrapping, so dragging near the bottom of a
day configured to extend past midnight couldn't produce a past-
midnight end time. Now clamps against the day's own (possibly
extended) dayEndMin and wraps the formatted clock time modulo 1440.

Also fixed dateRange() converting through toISOString() (UTC) to build
its date strings, which silently shifts dates back a day in any
timezone ahead of UTC (local midnight in CEST is still 22:00 the
previous day in UTC) -- it now reads the local calendar fields
directly. This affected the day-tab dates and PDF export's date range.

Verified live: created a 20:00-01:00 shift, confirmed via computed
style that it renders at the correct pixel position/height (560px
top, 280px height = exactly 5h at 56px/hour) spanning past midnight.

